Description: Don't fall back to focusing minimized windows
 MRUWindowList::visible() only skipped hidden windows, so when the active
 window was minimized or closed, Mir's fallback (refocus(), the minimize
 path of set_state) could pick a minimized window, and
 select_active_window() restored it. Minimizing two windows in a row
 brought the first one back; closing the last open window brought back a
 minimized one, even from another workspace. mutter never does that: a
 minimized window only comes back when the user asks for it. Explicit
 activation does not go through this list and still restores it.
Author: Umoja developers
Forwarded: not yet
Last-Update: 2026-11-16
---
--- a/src/miral/mru_window_list.cpp
+++ b/src/miral/mru_window_list.cpp
@@ -26,7 +26,13 @@
 bool visible(miral::Window const& window)
 {
     std::shared_ptr<mir::scene::Surface> const& surface{window};
-    return surface->state() != mir_window_state_hidden;
+    // Umoja: a minimized window is not a candidate for focus either. Mir's
+    // fallback (refocus(), minimizing the active window) used to pick one and
+    // select_active_window() restored it, so minimizing or closing a window
+    // brought a minimized one back, as mutter never does. Explicit
+    // activation does not go through this list and still restores it.
+    auto const state = surface->state();
+    return state != mir_window_state_hidden && state != mir_window_state_minimized;
 }
 }
 
